      "content": "$$u(a_7) = (\\bar{\\imath} + y\\bar{j} + xy\\bar{k})(1 + y^2 + x^2y^2)^{-1/2}.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 76,
      "topLeftY": 749,
      "bottomRightX": 112,
      "bottomRightY": 765,
      "content": "Thus",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 177,
      "topLeftY": 772,
      "bottomRightX": 448,
      "bottomRightY": 805,
      "content": "$$\\cos \\varphi = \\frac{xy}{((1 + x^2 + x^2y^2)(1 + y^2 + x^2y^2))^{1/2}}.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 76,
      "topLeftY": 810,
      "bottomRightX": 550,
      "bottomRightY": 846,
      "content": "By elementary calculus the maximum value of this expression is $\\frac{1}{2}$. Hence $\\Gamma_1$ is realizable if $0 \\leq \\cos \\varphi \\leq \\frac{1}{2}$, i.e., $0 \\leq \\sin \\theta \\leq \\frac{1}{2}$.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
